---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="How we pick" description="How vegan.place chooses its favorite vegan spots. The method behind the munching.">
  <div class="hero-wrap">
    <span class="float-veg" style="top: 20%; right: 10%; animation-delay: 0.5s;" aria-hidden="true">🥦</span>
    <span class="float-veg" style="bottom: 15%; right: 18%; animation-delay: 2s;" aria-hidden="true">🍓</span>
    <p class="hero-kicker">🧪 Our method (it's simple)</p>
    <h1 class="hero">How we pick <span class="hl">the good stuff.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every list on this site is built the same way: lots of reading, a healthy
      distrust of hype, and a monthly re-check. No advertisers, no affiliate links,
      no free-dessert bribes. Here's the whole recipe.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>The recipe 📝</h2></div>

  <div class="grid spots">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>1 · We read everything</h3>
      <p>Each month we dig through food press, local blogs, Reddit threads, and
      existing best-of lists for every live city. We read what people are actually
      saying, not what marketing departments paid for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2 · Consensus required</h3>
      <p>A spot only makes the list if it shows up across multiple independent sources.
      One glowing blog post is a data point. Five is a pattern. We trust patterns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>3 · Ratings are a filter, not a verdict</h3>
      <p>Rough bar: 4.4+ stars with serious review volume for established spots, a
      little slack for new openings with genuine buzz. The final call is editorial —
      numbers just get you in the door.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>4 · We write down why</h3>
      <p>Every entry gets a written justification. No silent inclusions, no unexplained
      rankings. If we can't say why a spot matters, it doesn't ship.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>5 · We re-check monthly</h3>
      <p>Taste goes stale. Every entry carries a last-checked date, and old entries get
      re-verified or cut. Restaurants close, chefs leave, quality drifts. This list is
      a living thing, not a monument.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>What this isn't 🚫</h2></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p><strong>Not exhaustive.</strong> This is a short list, not a phone book.</p>
    <p><strong>Not paid.</strong> Nobody can buy a rank. There is no sales team. There is barely a team.</p>
    <p><strong>Not every place with a veggie burger.</strong> If you want all of those, directories exist. This is the good stuff.</p>
  </div>

  <hr class="divider" />
  <p style="color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 600;">Disagree with a pick? Good. Strong opinions are the point — everything gets reconsidered monthly.</p>
</Base>
